<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa board offers 85,045 T wheat for export.</title>
<headline>S.Africa board offers 85,045 T wheat for export.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African Wheat Board said on Thursday it had made available 85,045 tonnes of surplus wheat for export to African countries only.  </p>
<p>The board said in a statement that the wheat, which was for delivery before May 31, 1997, was offered at a price of 895 rand a tonne, excluding VAT, for the BS1/BS2 grade and at 875 rand a tonne, VAT excluded, for the BL1/BL2 grade free on rail.</p>
<p>The wheat will be available in bulk form at a number of the board's depots, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
